  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This is Provence's summer soup. Vegetables, beans, and noodles simmer together in a plain broth, and then you stir in a big spoonful of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "pistou",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "pistou"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at the table. The pistou melts into the hot soup and changes everything. You can "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "blanch",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blanch"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " the green beans separately if you want them to stay bright, but it is not required."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Always add the pistou at the table, not into the pot. Heat kills the fresh basil flavour."
          }
        ]
      },
